Krita Nova 59 - Brush Panel: blending mode button, Opacity / Flow switch

- Below the "more" (3 dots) button, a button with two letters for the
  brush blending mode: the first two of its name ("Normal" -> "No"), and
  for the common painting modes their own, so they differ (Color Dodge
  "CD", Linear Burn "LB", Linear Dodge "LD", Linear Light "LL", Vivid Light
  "VL", Pin Light "PL", Hard Light "HL", Soft Light (Photoshop) "SL", Soft
  Light (SVG) "SS", Hard Mix "HM", Hard Mix (Photoshop) "HP", Hard Overlay
  "HO", Grain Merge / Extract "GM" / "GE", Darker / Lighter Color "DC" /
  "LC", Easy Burn / Dodge "EB" / "ED", Alpha Darken "AD", Divide "Dv",
  Dissolve "Ds", Copy "Cp", Bumpmap "Bm", Luminosity/Shine (SAI) "LS"). Tapping it opens the same
  blending mode list as before: it is the brush toolbar's blending mode
  combo box, moved out of the "more" popup and covered by the label box.
  The "more" popup no longer has the blending mode (alpha lock and reload
  stay there).
- Below the bottom slider, an "O" / "F" button: it switches the slider
  between Opacity and Flow (its letter and tooltip follow). The choice is
  remembered (kritarc [KritaNova] brushPanelSliderIsFlow).
- Both buttons look the same: a rounded box with a thin outline and bold
  letters (paintNovaLetterBox).

